1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''The 117th Ancestor: 譚朝安 (Tán Cháo Ān)''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT The 117th generation Tan ancestor was 朝安 (Cháo Ān). He was the sixth son of Baocang（伯倉).
2 CONT
2 CONT He had been studying hard since he was young. He went to the palace at the age of 21. He tried several examinations, but failed at getting degrees. During the 庆历 (Qìng Lì) period of Emperor Renzong (仁宗) of the Song Dynasty (or in 
2 CONC 1040's), he followed his father to Guangzhou (广州) where he was managing the Anchang Ironing Shop. He then opened an ironing shop in Guangzhou. He was smart and refused to collaborate with insurgents. He helped the army to fight wi
2 CONC th these insurgents by providing expenditures. Yuanjiang (元絳), the Director of Salt in Guangdong, reported to the Emperor about the help of Chaoan. Chaoan was awarded as a grand master of administration and responsible for the tax
2 CONC ation of salt.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father lived in Pingshanli (平出里), Renhua (仁化). He moved to live in Yancang (塩仓), Guangzhou. His descendants moved to counties, Xinhui (新会) county, Kaiping (开平) county, and Taishan (台山) counties. He was born around 11AM-1PM on 
2 CONC the 21st of the eighth month in the second year of Tiansheng (天圣) period of Emperor Renzong (仁宗) of the Song Dynasty (or in 1024 AD) and passed away at 7-9AM on the 21st of the ninth month in the seventh year of Yuanfeng (元丰) peri
2 CONC od of Emperor Shengzong (神宗) of the Song Dynasty (or in 1084 AD). He died at age 61. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, Xu (徐), was born about 1PM - 3PM on the 3rd of the first month in the first year of Tiansheng (天圣) period of Emperor Renzong in the Song Dynasty (or in 1023AD) and passed away in the eighth year of Yuanfeng (元丰) period o
2 CONC f Shenzong (神宗) in the Song Dynasty (or in 1085AD). She died at age 63. Both were buried at Huangye (皇爷) hill, Shangyuangang (上元风) village, Fanyu (番禺). The grave was re-built in the fifth year of Guangxu (光緒) period in Qing () Dyn
2 CONC asty (or in 1879). One temple was built at 3 Xiaomazhan, Huiai Road, Guangzhou. The temple was named Chaoan Study (朝安书院). It was re-built in the 19th year of Guangxu period in the Qing Dynasty (or in 1893). Every February and Augu
2 CONC st are the seasons to do memorials. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He had three sons, first Daweng (达翁), second Yuanweng (元翁), and third Luweng (陆翁).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Google Translation:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 第117位祖先：譚朝安（TánCháoĀn）
2 CONT
2 CONT 第117代譚祖先是朝安（ChaáoĀn）。他是寶倉的第六個兒子。
2 CONT
2 CONT 他從小就開始努力學習。他在21歲時去了宮殿。他嘗試了幾次考試，但沒有獲得學位。在宋代仁宗皇帝的慶曆（10月）期間，他跟隨父親去了廣州，在那裡他管理著安昌熨燙店。然後，他在廣州開了一家熨燙店。他很聰明，拒絕與叛亂分子合作。他通過提供支出幫助軍隊與這些叛亂分子作戰。廣東鹽業局局長元江向皇帝匯報了潮安的幫助。潮安縣被授予行政管理碩士稱號，並負責鹽的徵稅工作。
2 CONT
2 CONT 他的父親住在仁化的平出裡。他搬到廣州Yan倉居住。他的後代遷至縣，新會縣，開平縣和台山縣。他出生於宋仁宗天聖第二年（即公元1024年）的第八個月的第21個上午11點至下午1點，並於當年7點至9點去世。宋神宗的元豐元年第七年九月21日（或公元1084年）。他享年61歲。
2 CONT
2 CONT 他的妻子徐（Xu）生於宋朝（或公元1023年）天皇仁宗天聖元年第一年的第一個月的下午3點至3點，並於第八年去世。宋（或在1085AD）神宗的元豐年。她去世了，享年63歲。兩人都被葬在番禺上元崗村的皇爺山上。該墳墓是在清光緒五年（或1879年）重建的。在廣州市惠愛路小馬山3號建造了一座廟宇。這座寺廟被命名為朝安書院。它是在清光緒19年（或1893年）重建的。每年的二月和八月是紀念活動的季節。
2 CONT
2 CONT 他有三個兒子，第一個是達翁（Daweng），第二個是元翁（Yuanweng），第三個是陸翁（Luong）。
