1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (English Translation via Google Translate)
2 CONT
2 CONT Foreword:
2 CONT
2 CONT De Chao Weng, the third son of Lord Tianlin, is the ancestor of the Tan surname in the Jinkeng area of ​​Taicheng.
2 CONT
2 CONT De Chao whose personal name is Mu Jing was born in the Ming Dynasty. The ancestral concubine was a son of the Mai family in Huangzhugan, and a woman married with the surname Chen in Pinggang. The ancestor died on the third day of 
2 CONC May and was buried in the Qianhaixiang of Aobei Mountain. Later, he served as Jongweng in the capital. He was given to Zheng Shilang and the concubine gave a gift to a Confucian. He died on the second day of February and was burie
2 CONC d in the tomb of the ancestor of Aotou Mountain in Baishui. Dry to the right. The name of the mountain: The nine generations do not help Li Li. Eight generations of a single pass.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Original)
2 CONT
2 CONT 前言:
2 CONT
2 CONT 天麟公之三子德超翁是台城筋坑地區譚姓之始祖。
2 CONT
2 CONT 德超字慕景，明朝歲貢生，官任雲南曲靖軍民府，後陞陸梁州同知。祖妣是黃竹竿里麥氏生一子迥翁，女一人嫁平崗里陳姓。祖卒于五月初三日，葬于凹背山之乾亥向，后以迥翁任京職，贈征仕郎，妣贈儒人，卒于二月初二日，葬于白水凹頭山之祖墓右乾亥向。山名：九代不扶黎犁。八代單傳。
