1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (English translation via Google Translate)
2 CONT
2 CONT The third generation ancestor Jongweng was born in Yisi (1425 AD), the first year of Renzong Hongxi in the Ming Dynasty. He was born in Xinhui Yixian. He has served as Jiyangwei in Beijing. He was promoted to Tongzhi in Luliangzho
2 CONC u, the military and civilian residence of Qujing, Yunnan. He is good at learning Chinese, especially good at poetry. Marrying Chen gave birth to a son, Yu Haosheng, and a daughter married to Chen. After his death on the tenth day 
2 CONC of March, he gave him a gift to a Confucian, and then married Chen and gave birth to a daughter. The ancestor died in the eighteenth year of Emperor Xiaozong of the Ming Dynasty in Yichou (1506 AD) in November. One day in autumn, 
2 CONC the tomb was buried in the original Xunxiang of Zixia Mountain. The ancestor of the Chen family was buried on the tenth day of October, and the death and former concubine of Weng Chen were both buried in the original Xunxiang of F
2 CONC ulu.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Original)
2 CONT
2 CONT 三世祖迥翁字謙目，生于明朝仁宗洪熙元年乙巳（公元一四二五年），補新會邑庠生，歷任北京濟陽衛經歷，升任雲南曲靖軍民府陸梁州同知，好學能文，尤長于詩。娶陳氏生一子諱浩生，一女嫁陳氏，妣卒于三月初十後贈儒人，繼娶陳氏生一女。祖卒于明孝宗弘治十八年乙丑（公元一五〇六年）十一月。一日秋，享毒八十一有一，墓葬于紫霞山之原巽向。陳氏祖葬於十月初十，而卒與翁之前妣陳氏俱葬于龍卷倒地芙蘆之原巽向。
