1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =譚裔均 (Tán Yì Jūn)=
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''譚裔均 (Tán Yì Jūn)''' (birth date and death date unknown) was born in Changxing (常興村), Jinkeng Township, Jiangmen, Taishan County, Guangdong Province, Qing Dynasty (清朝).
2 CONT
2 CONT His birth name is unknown, but I speculate his name might have been similar to my paternal great grandfather's name, probably 譚森发, 譚松栢, 譚森发, 譚森栢 or 譚桑松.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family:==
2 CONT
2 CONT 譚裔均 (Tán Yì Jūn)'s father, 譚文楫 (Tán Wén Jí), had two wives -【(李)】譚氏 and【(陳)】譚氏.
2 CONT
2 CONT 譚裔均 (Tán Yì Jūn)'s younger paternal half brother, 譚松发 (Tōng Fāt) came from the second wife【(陳氏)】, and 譚裔均 (Tán Yì Jūn) came from the first wife 【(李氏)】. Their mother's names are unknown. It is unknown if he had any female siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Other Names:==
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Montreal Lovell's Directory Guide, 譚裔均 (Tán Yì Jūn)'s other names might have been Sang Tom, Sing Tom, Sam Tom, and/or Conrad Tom.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to his eldest and only surviving daughter, 譚寶鳳 (Bǎo Fèng), my second great uncle's marriage name, 譚裔均 (Tán Yì Jūn) was chosen for him by the village elders upon marriage, with the 裔 character from the Tan Clan Generation
2 CONC al Poem.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Adult Life:==
2 CONT
2 CONT Not much is known about '譚裔均 (Tán Yì Jūn) other than stories told by his only surviving daughter, 譚寶鳳 (Bǎo Fèng), who currently lives in San Francisco, California. Unfortunately, she never met her father in person, stating that he
2 CONC  was afraid of returning to China due to the lack of food and potential starvation.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is speculated that he might be 5-10 years older than my paternal great-grandfather, 譚松发 (Tōng Fāt), and probably moved to Montreal, Quebec Province Canada, to work as a laundryman between the years of 1896 - 1907 AD.
2 CONT
2 CONT After my paternal great grandfather, 譚松发 (Tōng Fāt)/譚裔益 (Tán Yì Yì)/Edward Tom passed away from tuberculosis on Sunday, May 05, 1935, my second great uncle continued to send money to my paternal grandfather, 譚沃榮 (Wò Róng) and his 
2 CONC mother, 譚坤芳 (Kūn Fāng), but his wife, 陳银伏 (Yín Fú), intercepted the money and didn't offer much help to my paternal grandfather, which I believe most likely contributed and perpetuated the poverty my paternal grandfather experienc
2 CONC ed while growing up.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other family stories state that my second great uncle, 譚裔均 (Tán Yì Jūn), and my great grandfather, 譚松发 (Tōng Fāt)/譚裔益 (Tán Yì Yì)/Edward Tom, owned a restaurant together, but this is unconfirmed.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to his eldest and surviving daughter, 譚裔均 (Tán Yì Jūn), was afraid of returning to China and suffering from starvation, stating that there was a lot to eat in Montreal / life was better there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Death:==
2 CONT
2 CONT According to his daughter, 譚寶鳳 (Bǎo Fèng), 譚裔均 (Tán Yì Jūn) passed away in the 1950s from an unknown illness, and his daughter was informed by someone whom she referred to as a tall man.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, according to Adrian King-Edwards of The Word Bookstore, Adrian remembers interacting with the elderly proprietor of Sing Tom Laundry, so it's speculated that the elderly proprietor was 譚裔均 (Tán Yì Jūn), and as such, I ass
2 CONC ume he probably passed away between the years of 1975 and 1980.
2 CONT
2 CONT As of Monday, April 24, 2023, it is presumed that 譚裔均 (Yì Jūn) was interred in Mount Royal Cemetery in Montreal, Quebec Province, but my searches have been fruitless.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Last Updated on Monday, April 24, 2023===
